{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l1nco06v","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 2 Offline","year":2013,"examDate":2013,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"thermodynamics","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","topic":"fundamentals-of-thermodynamics","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pthe-succeeding-operations-that-enable-this-transformation-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-hrdbtxnxspzv2j9p","content":"<p>The succeeding operations that enable this transformation of states are</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Heating, cooling, heating, cooling."},{"identifier":"B","content":"Cooling, heating, cooling, heating."},{"identifier":"C","content":"Heating, cooling, cooling, heating."},{"identifier":"D","content":"Cooling, heating, heating, cooling."}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p>From the graph, as the term pV increases, the temperature increases; and when pV decreases the temperature decreases.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1qnui3o/9e4cbcec-3a48-4163-b578-072185d6c3d6/7872f730-b75b-11ec-9370-27e75f4b6a7c/file-1l1qnui3p.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l1qnui3o/9e4cbcec-3a48-4163-b578-072185d6c3d6/7872f730-b75b-11ec-9370-27e75f4b6a7c/file-1l1qnui3p.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Thermodynamics Question 24 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l1qnui3o/9e4cbcec-3a48-4163-b578-072185d6c3d6/7872f730-b75b-11ec-9370-27e75f4b6a7c/file-1l1qnui3p.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l1qnui3o/9e4cbcec-3a48-4163-b578-072185d6c3d6/7872f730-b75b-11ec-9370-27e75f4b6a7c/file-1l1qnui3p.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1qnui3o/9e4cbcec-3a48-4163-b578-072185d6c3d6/7872f730-b75b-11ec-9370-27e75f4b6a7c/file-1l